version: 2.0.0
description: |
  Human-facing `paradigm skill` CLI (Skills Phase 1, T-2026-09-26-002). A thin
  skin over paradigm-mcp's #skill-loader / #skill-projector / !skill-used
  modules, imported by relative path (task-cli precedent). Agent-owned SKILL.md
  sources live in <root>/.paradigm/skills/<id>/ (project) › ~/.paradigm/skills/<id>/
  (global); projection is one-way into ~/.claude/skills/pdg-<id>/ (or
  <root>/.claude/skills with --target project), certified-only unless
  --allow-provisional. Output goes through cli-output.ts helpers.
components:
  skill-cli:
    description: |
      `paradigm skill` verbs — list [--agent] [--json] (id, version, steward,
      trust, computed status, scope; `*` marks unverified third-party pins),
      show <id> (frontmatter, resolved pins table, cited notebooks), lint
      [<id>|--all] (exit 1 on errors), check <id> [--tools <tools/list dump>]
      (paradigm_* pins hashed against listToolDefinitions()), project
      [<id>|--all] [--target user|project] [--allow-provisional] [--dry-run]
      [--tools], adopt <id> (downstream edits → source, patch+1, provisional),
      certify <id> (see $skill-certification), sync-global [--force]
      [--dry-run] (bundled templates/skills → ~/.paradigm/skills, skips
      existing), and the hidden record-usage (reads a PostToolUse `Skill` hook
      payload on stdin; silent, never fails) that appends !skill-used rows.
      v7.11: import <pack-id>:<skill-id> [--global] — interactive-TTY only
      (refuses non-TTY), prints allowed-tools + scripts/ list, requires the
      id typed back, then #skill-loader importPackSkill (provisional, source
      pack). list/show render scope `pack:<packId>`; project --all skips pack
      skills (they never project).
      v7.11 fix pass: import hashes the pack skill (computeContentHash) before the confirmation prompt and passes it as expectedHash, so a pack changed mid-prompt is refused (content-changed).
    type: command
    file: index.ts
    tags:
      - skills
      - cli
    signals:
      - '!skill-used'
  skill-sync-global:
    description: 'resolveBundledSkillsDir() probes dist/ and src/ layouts for <packageRoot>/templates/skills (shipped via package.json files: templates). skillSyncGlobalCommand copies each bundled <id>/ dir into ~/.paradigm/skills/<id>/; an existing destination is skipped unless --force (user customizations are never destroyed by a normal sync).'
    type: command
    file: sync-global.ts
    tags:
      - skills
  skill-certify:
    description: 'CLI-only founder sign-off implementing $skill-certification. TTY gate first (process.stdin.isTTY), then evaluateCertification with lint + pins + scenarios (optionally --scenario filtered), then the founder (git user.name) types the skill id. Writes the certification block via applyCertification + writeSkill and appends a kind:skill row with appendClassroomCertification(buildSkillCertRow(...)). Never an MCP tool — agents cannot self-certify.'
    type: command
    file: certify.ts
    tags:
      - skills
      - certification
flows:
  skill-certification:
    description: |
      $skill-certification — (1) steward proposes: trust provisional + lint
      clean; (2) a PEER (≠ steward) authors a scenario in
      .paradigm/curriculum/scenarios/ with `fixture:` (planted defect), a probe
      {agent: <peer>, learning_ref: "skill:<id>@<ver>"} and expected.must:
      survive; (3) the skill is run against the fixture and a human-confirmed
      `survived` outcome is appended for term "skill:<id>@<ver>"; (4)
      `paradigm skill certify` verifies all of it plus no stale pin and an
      interactive TTY, and the founder types the id; (5) the SKILL.md gains
      `certification` + trust certified (source of truth, GLOBAL, records
      project); (6) a kind:skill classroom-certifications row is appended. The
      key skill:<id>@<ver> is identical across probe, cert row and usage row.
    steps:
      - '#skill-cli'
      - '#skill-loader'
      - '#scenario-loader'
      - '#classroom-certifications'
